IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art8-register`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`

-- g3-tests-art8-time.l4: the periods of Article 8 -- "the most recent year" of 8(3)(j) (P3) and "10 years" of 8(6) (P4) -- and the Minister's powers by Order.
-- Expected values are decided from the text and from the conventions registered as forks F3.1, F3.2, F3.4, F3.5 and F3.7.  Both sides of every date edge are asserted.

§ `Tests of the periods of Article 8`

fav MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`

§§ `Article 8(3)(j): has the annual return for the most recent year been sent?`

GIVEN lastDay IS A DATE
      sent IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
`a return for the year ending` lastDay `, sent on` sent MEANS
    `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH
        `last day of the year to which it relates` IS lastDay
        `date sent` IS sent

GIVEN fy IS A MAYBE DATE
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
GIVETH A `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))`
`return facts: the financial year ends` fy `, returns` returns MEANS
    `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` WITH
        `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS fy
        `annual returns sent` IS returns

-- The 2025 return of Alpha (registered 1 March 2019), sent on 15 February 2026.
`the 2025 return` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2026 2 15)
`the 2026 return` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2027 1 5)
`the 2024 return` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2024 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2025 2 1)

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` interp returns day MEANS
    `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` interp `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` day (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` returns)

-- The calendar year that has most recently ended.  On 30 June 2026 it is 2025: the return for 2025 was sent on 15 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2025 return`) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- The day it was sent is in; the day before is out (the return is not sent until 15 February).
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2025 return`) (YMD 2026 2 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2025 return`) (YMD 2026 2 14)
-- No return at all, or a return for another year.
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav EMPTY (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2024 return`) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- The last day of 2026: the year 2026 has not ended on that day (it ends at its close), so the most recent year is still 2025.
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2025 return`) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2026 return`) (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- The first day of 2027: 2026 has ended; the 2025 return no longer answers, the 2026 return does once sent (5 January 2027).
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2025 return`) (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2026 return`) (YMD 2027 1 4)
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2026 return`) (YMD 2027 1 5)
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` fav (LIST `the 2025 return`, `the 2026 return`) (YMD 2027 1 5)

-- F3.7: the year in progress.  On 30 June 2026 it is 2026.
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` `interpretation F3.7 reading B` (LIST `the 2025 return`) (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` `interpretation F3.7 reading B` (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- On 31 December 2026 the year in progress is still 2026; on 1 January 2027 it is 2027.
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` `interpretation F3.7 reading B` (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` `interpretation F3.7 reading B` (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on a calendar year` `interpretation F3.7 reading B` (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2027 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2027 1 1))) (YMD 2027 1 1)

-- F3.2: a charity with a 30 June year-end that sent its return for the year to 30 June 2026 on 1 September 2026, asked on 1 February 2027.
`the return for the year to 30 June 2026` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 6 30) `, sent on` (YMD 2026 9 1)

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` interp returns day MEANS
    `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` interp `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` day (`return facts: the financial year ends` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)) `, returns` returns)

-- Calendar year: the most recent is 2026 (ended 31 December 2026); the return is for the year to 30 June 2026, which is not that year.
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` fav (LIST `the return for the year to 30 June 2026`) (YMD 2027 2 1)
-- Financial year: the most recent to have ended is the year to 30 June 2026, and the return for it was sent.
#ASSERT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 30 June 2026`) (YMD 2027 2 1)
-- Edges of the financial year: on 30 June 2026 itself that year has not ended, so the year to 30 June 2025 is the most recent.
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 30 June 2026`) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- On 1 July 2026 it has ended, but the return was not sent until 1 September.
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 30 June 2026`) (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 30 June 2026`) (YMD 2026 8 31)
#ASSERT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 30 June 2026`) (YMD 2026 9 1)
-- The return for the year to 30 June 2025 answers on 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Alpha with a 30 June year-end has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2025 6 30) `, sent on` (YMD 2025 8 1))) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- The financial year was asked about but its end is not given: the Law does not say what the end is.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` `interpretation F3.2 reading B` `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` (YMD 2027 2 1) (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` EMPTY)
-- The other readings of "year" never need the financial year-end.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` fav `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` (YMD 2027 2 1) (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` EMPTY)

-- F3.2: the twelve months from each anniversary of registration (registered 1 March 2019): the years end on 28 February, or 29 February in a leap year.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` interp returns day MEANS
    `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` interp `Alpha, registered on 1 March 2019` day (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` returns)

`the return for the year to 28 February 2026` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 2 28) `, sent on` (YMD 2026 3 10)
`the return for the year to 29 February 2024` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2024 2 29) `, sent on` (YMD 2024 3 10)
`the return for the year to 28 February 2024` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2024 2 28) `, sent on` (YMD 2024 3 10)

#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2026`) (YMD 2027 2 1)
-- The year to 28 February 2026 has not ended on 28 February 2026, and has on 1 March 2026 (and the return was sent on 10 March).
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2026`) (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2026`) (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2026`) (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- A leap year: the anniversary of 1 March 2019 in 2024 is 1 March 2024, so the year ends on 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 29 February 2024`) (YMD 2024 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Alpha has sent its return on an anniversary year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2024`) (YMD 2024 3 15)

-- F3.5 with F3.2 reading C: a charity registered on 29 February 2020.  The anniversary in 2021 is 28 February (the day moves back) or 1 March (it rolls forward),
-- so the year to the day before it ends on 27 February or on 28 February 2021.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the leap-day charity has sent its return` interp returns day MEANS
    `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` interp (`a charity registered on` (YMD 2020 2 29)) day (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` returns)

`the return for the year to 27 February 2021` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2021 2 27) `, sent on` (YMD 2021 3 10)
`the return for the year to 28 February 2021` MEANS `a return for the year ending` (YMD 2021 2 28) `, sent on` (YMD 2021 3 10)

#ASSERT `the leap-day charity has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 27 February 2021`) (YMD 2021 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `the leap-day charity has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2021`) (YMD 2021 3 15)
#ASSERT `the leap-day charity has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading C with F3.5 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 28 February 2021`) (YMD 2021 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `the leap-day charity has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading C with F3.5 reading B` (LIST `the return for the year to 27 February 2021`) (YMD 2021 3 15)

-- A charity's own years, not the calendar's: the registration date decides whether a year is the charity's.
GIVEN registered IS A DATE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
      returns IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a charity registered on` registered `has sent its return` interp returns day MEANS
    `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` interp (`a charity registered on` registered) day (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` returns)

-- Registered on the last day of 2025: 2025 ended on that day, so it is a year of the charity.  Asked on 1 January 2026: the answer is "not sent", not a refusal.
#ASSERT NOT `a charity registered on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `has sent its return` fav EMPTY (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `a charity registered on` (YMD 2025 12 31) `has sent its return` fav (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2025 12 31))) (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Registered on 1 January 2026: 2025 ended before it was registered, so no year of the charity has ended on 2 January 2026: the Law does not say what is entered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` fav (`a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 1 1)) (YMD 2026 1 2) (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` EMPTY)
-- Registered on 1 March 2026 and asked on 30 June 2026: the same.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` fav (`a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) (YMD 2026 6 30) (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` EMPTY)
-- After the end of 2026, it is the charity's first year to have ended.
#ASSERT NOT `a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `has sent its return` fav EMPTY (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `has sent its return` fav (LIST (`a return for the year ending` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, sent on` (YMD 2027 1 1))) (YMD 2027 1 1)
-- The year in progress needs no completed year, so there is no refusal in the first year.
#ASSERT NOT `a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `has sent its return` `interpretation F3.7 reading B` EMPTY (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- Anniversary years in the first year of registration: nothing has ended until the first anniversary has passed.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 8(3)(j) the registered charity has sent its annual return for the most recent year` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` (`a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) (YMD 2027 2 28) (`return facts: the financial year ends` NOTHING `, returns` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `a charity registered on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `has sent its return` `interpretation F3.2 reading C` EMPTY (YMD 2027 3 1)
